#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_filtered:3 of
msgid ""
"The quadratic nonlinearity acts on a weighted combination of the two most"
" recent state samples, ``z = c_0 · x_1 + c_1 · x_2``, rather than on a "
"single sample. This is the smallest non-trivial case of "
":func:`henon_order_n`."
msgstr ""
"The quadratic nonlinearity acts on a weighted combination of the two most"
" recent state samples, ``z = c_0 · x_1 + c_1 · x_2``, rather than on a "
"single sample. This is the smallest non-trivial case of "
":func:`henon_order_n`."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_filtered:11
#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_filtered:12
#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:19
#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:20 of
msgid "Hénon parameters."
msgstr "Hénon parameters."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_filtered:13
#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_filtered:16 of
msgid ""
"FIR filter coefficients. With ``(c0, c1) = (1, 0)`` the map reduces "
"exactly to :func:`henon_generalised` — this equivalence is exercised by "
"``TestHenonFiltered`` in the test suite."
msgstr ""
"FIR filter coefficients. With ``(c0, c1) = (1, 0)`` the map reduces "
"exactly to :func:`henon_generalised` — this equivalence is exercised by "
"``TestHenonFiltered`` in the test suite."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:3 of
msgid ""
"The system dimension ``N_c`` is inferred from ``len(fir_coeffs)``. At "
"each step, the carrier output is the filtered state component ``x[2]``, "
"and the next iterate is computed by :func:`_henon_n4_step_inplace`."
msgstr ""
"The system dimension ``N_c`` is inferred from ``len(fir_coeffs)``. At "
"each step, the carrier output is the filtered state component ``x[2]``, "
"and the next iterate is computed by :func:`_henon_n4_step_inplace`."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:8 of
msgid ""
"The ``driving`` parameter lets callers override the nonlinear input: when"
" ``driving=None`` the map runs autonomously (``s = x[2]``); when "
"``driving`` is provided the map is forced by that external signal. This "
"is used by the transmitter (self-driven) vs. the receiver (driven by the "
"received signal)."
msgstr ""
"The ``driving`` parameter lets callers override the nonlinear input: when"
" ``driving=None`` the map runs autonomously (``s = x[2]``); when "
"``driving`` is provided the map is forced by that external signal. This "
"is used by the transmitter (self-driven) vs. the receiver (driven by the "
"received signal)."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:14 of
msgid "Number of iterations. The output state has shape ``(Nc, steps + 1)``."
msgstr "Number of iterations. The output state has shape ``(Nc, steps + 1)``."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:16 of
msgid "FIR filter coefficients, shape ``(Nc,)``. Must have ``Nc >= 3``."
msgstr "FIR filter coefficients, shape ``(Nc,)``. Must have ``Nc >= 3``."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:17 of
msgid ""
"Optional explicit initial state, shape ``(Nc,)``. If ``None``, a random "
"state is drawn from ``Uniform(0, 0.5)`` per component."
msgstr ""
"Optional explicit initial state, shape ``(Nc,)``. If ``None``, a random "
"state is drawn from ``Uniform(0, 0.5)`` per component."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:21 of
msgid ""
"Optional external driving signal, shape ``(steps,)``. When provided, "
"replaces the self-driving term at each iteration."
msgstr ""
"Optional external driving signal, shape ``(steps,)``. When provided, "
"replaces the self-driving term at each iteration."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:23 of
msgid ""
"RNG seed used when ``x0=None`` to pick the random initial condition. Has "
"no effect if ``x0`` is provided."
msgstr ""
"RNG seed used when ``x0=None`` to pick the random initial condition. Has "
"no effect if ``x0`` is provided."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:26 of
msgid ""
"* **state** (*ndarray, shape (Nc, steps + 1)*) -- Full state trajectory. "
"Column 0 is the initial condition. * **output** (*ndarray, shape "
"(steps,)*) -- Carrier signal ``x[2][n]`` for ``n = 0, …, steps − 1``."
msgstr ""
"* **state** (*ndarray, shape (Nc, steps + 1)*) -- Full state trajectory. "
"Column 0 is the initial condition. * **output** (*ndarray, shape "
"(steps,)*) -- Carrier signal ``x[2][n]`` for ``n = 0, …, steps − 1``."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:26 of
msgid ""
"**state** (*ndarray, shape (Nc, steps + 1)*) -- Full state trajectory. "
"Column 0 is the initial condition."
msgstr ""
"**state** (*ndarray, shape (Nc, steps + 1)*) -- Full state trajectory. "
"Column 0 is the initial condition."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_order_n:27 of
msgid ""
"**output** (*ndarray, shape (steps,)*) -- Carrier signal ``x[2][n]`` for "
"``n = 0, …, steps − 1``."
msgstr ""
"**output** (*ndarray, shape (steps,)*) -- Carrier signal ``x[2][n]`` for "
"``n = 0, …, steps − 1``."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:3 of
msgid ""
"Iterates the generalised Hénon form ``x[n+1] = a - xf[n]^2 + b * y[n]``, "
"``y[n+1] = x[n]``, where ``xf`` is the current output of an FIR filter "
"applied to the state history."
msgstr ""
"Iterates the generalised Hénon form ``x[n+1] = a - xf[n]^2 + b * y[n]``, "
"``y[n+1] = x[n]``, where ``xf`` is the current output of an FIR filter "
"applied to the state history."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:7 of
msgid "Number of samples to produce."
msgstr "Number of samples to produce."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:8
#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:9 of
msgid "Hénon map parameters (default: 1.4, 0.3)."
msgstr "Hénon map parameters (default: 1.4, 0.3)."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:10 of
msgid "FIR filter order (number of coefficients)."
msgstr "FIR filter order (number of coefficients)."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:11 of
msgid "Normalised cutoff frequency in (0, 1)."
msgstr "Normalised cutoff frequency in (0, 1)."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:12 of
msgid "SciPy window name (e.g. ``\"hamming\"``, ``\"kaiser\"``)."
msgstr "SciPy window name (e.g. ``\"hamming\"``, ``\"kaiser\"``)."

#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.maps.henon_fir_sequence:14 of
msgid "Chaotic samples."
msgstr "Chaotic samples."

